# web888d command line. Settings belong in the configuration file on the
# configuration partition (ext4, mounted at /config): /config/web888d.toml.
# A missing file means defaults; `web888d serve --print-config` prints all
# keys with their current values, as a template. Changes are picked up
# within seconds (or `systemctl reload web888d`); radio/HPSDR/listen
# settings say they need a restart.
#
# The web UI's self-signed certificate is kept in /config/web888d. The
# bitstream comes from /usr/share/web888 (package web888-bitstream,
# `[radio] bitstream = "auto"`); to try another, put it on the boot
# partition (FAT, read-only at /boot) and set `bitstream = "/boot/<file>.bit"`.
WEB888D_ARGS="serve --config /config/web888d.toml --state-dir /config/web888d"
